---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { PROPERTIES } from "../lib/site";

const consulting = PROPERTIES.consulting;
---

<BaseLayout
  title=""
  description="Texas Movement Consulting turns messy operations and AI projects into predictable systems. Scoped diagnostics, systems builds, and retainers for founders."
  path="/"
>
  <style>
    .hero {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--hero), var(--hero-soft));
    }

    .hero-inner {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 52px;
      align-items: center;
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .hero-inner {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 32px;
      }
    }

    .hero-tagline {
      font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .hero-body {
      font-size: 1.02rem;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    .hero-ctas {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .hero-note {
      font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .hero-figure {
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 18px 18px 14px;
      background: rgba(255, 247, 238, 0.64);
    }

    .hero-figure-inner {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: auto auto;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .hero-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 10px;
      font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
    }

    .hero-node {
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 10px 10px 9px;
      background: var(--paper);
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
      min-height: 84px;
    }

    .hero-node-label {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .hero-node--source {
      border-color: var(--tension);
    }

    .hero-node--terminal {
      border-color: var(--compression);
    }

    .hero-caption {
      margin-top: 8px;
      font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      text-align: right;
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section id="overview" class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="hero-tagline">STRATEGY &middot; SYSTEMS &middot; AI WORKFLOWS.</div>
        <h1>Turn a messy problem into a system you can run.</h1>
        <p class="hero-body">
          Texas Movement Consulting is the systems and AI consulting arm of Texas Movement International. It is for
          founders, operators, and organizations with real stakes who need clearer workflows, better decisions, and
          tighter execution.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-body">
          It reduces founder-dependence and stalled projects by starting with a scoped diagnostic, engineering systems
          that hold under load, and documenting decisions so they stand up to scrutiny. It connects directly to Texas
          Movement&rsquo;s media, performance, and IP defense lanes, so consulting output compounds instead of sitting as
          a one-off deck.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a class="btn" href="#engagements"> See engagement tiers <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> </a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/start">
            {consulting.primaryCta.label} <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-note">SYSTEMS-FIRST &middot; DOCUMENTED &middot; BUILT TO COMPOUND WITH TEXAS MOVEMENT INTERNATIONAL</div>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-figure">
        <div class="hero-figure-inner">
          <div class="hero-grid">
            <div class="hero-node hero-node--source">
              <div class="hero-node-label">Diagnostics</div>
              <div>30-day systems and AI diagnostic to map how work, information, and money move through your company.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-node">
              <div class="hero-node-label">Systems build</div>
              <div>Engineer workflows, AI-assisted processes, and decision paths that hold under review and under load.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-node hero-node--terminal">
              <div class="hero-node-label">Operator retainer</div>
              <div>Embedded execution partner for founders who need ongoing decision support and systems stewardship.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-caption">FIG. 02 &mdash; CONSULTING LANE &middot; DIAGNOSTIC &rarr; SYSTEM &rarr; OPERATIONS</div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who it's for -->
  <section id="who" class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">WHO IT&rsquo;S FOR</div>
        <h2>Serious founders and operators with real stakes.</h2>
        <p>
          Best fit: founders and operators running 1&ndash;20 person companies&mdash;service businesses, boutiques, clinics,
          agencies, and teams&mdash;with real revenue at stake and operations held together by willpower instead of
          systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is for organizations already in motion that need structure, not for idea-stage projects or vague &ldquo;help
          us figure out everything&rdquo; requests. Work here is scoped around constraints, timelines, and measurable
          outcomes.
        </p>
        <p>It is a poor fit for hype-driven campaigns, endless discovery, or engagements with no clear owner or outcome.</p>
      </div>

      <aside id="keynote" class="panel-highlight">
        <h3>Keynote speaking at the systems layer.</h3>
        <p>
          For conferences, company offsites, and serious rooms that need live systems thinking, keynote speaking runs
          through founder Alexander Mathai&rsquo;s authority profile.
        </p>
        <p>
          Topics cover systems for founders, AI and operations, economic leverage, and building multi-lane companies
          that compound instead of fragment. Keynotes are scoped like consulting work&mdash;clear constraints, outcomes,
          and accountability.
        </p>
        <p class="cta-link">
          <a href={PROPERTIES.founder.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Go to AlexanderMathai.com for keynote speaking &rarr;
          </a>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section id="how" class="section section--panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</div>
      <h2>Systems-first. Documented. Built to hold under load.</h2>
      <div class="cards-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-label">Principle</div>
          <div class="card-title">Systems before narrative.</div>
          <p class="card-body">
            We map the actual flows&mdash;work, information, money&mdash;before telling a story about them. The narrative
            follows the system, not the other way around.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-label">Principle</div>
          <div class="card-title">Document the decisions.</div>
          <p class="card-body">
            Every engagement produces a record that explains why decisions were made, how they connect, and what needs
            to be monitored so the system keeps working.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-label">Principle</div>
          <div class="card-title">Legally in-bounds.</div>
          <p class="card-body">
            Work stays inside systems and operations. It supports your counsel; it does not replace legal, tax, or
            medical advice.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-label">Principle</div>
          <div class="card-title">Built for serious work.</div>
          <p class="card-body">
            Engagements are scoped with real constraints, stakes, and timelines. This is not casual coaching or
            speculative brainstorming.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Engagements & pricing -->
  <section id="engagements" class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">ENGAGEMENTS &amp; PRICING</div>
      <h2>Three clear tiers for systems and AI work.</h2>
      <p>
        Engagements start with a scoped diagnostic, then move into systems build and, where it makes sense, an operator
        retainer. Pricing reflects the depth of work and the stakes involved.
      </p>

      <div class="cards-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-label">Tier 1 &middot; Diagnostic</div>
          <div class="card-title">30-Day Systems &amp; AI Diagnostic.</div>
          <p class="card-body">
            Map how work, information, and money move through your company. Identify friction, owner-dependence, and
            critical failure points. Return a prioritized systems plan with timelines, owners, and key decisions.
          </p>
          <div class="price-line">$1,500&ndash;$3,000 &middot; one-time &middot; 30 days.</div>
          <div class="cta-link">
            <a href="/start">See how a diagnostic starts &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-label">Tier 2 &middot; Systems build</div>
          <div class="card-title">Implementation sprints &amp; AI workflows.</div>
          <p class="card-body">
            Design and stand up systems and AI-assisted workflows based on the diagnostic findings. We co-own
            implementation with your team and document the system so it can be audited and adjusted.
          </p>
          <div class="price-line">$12,000&ndash;$25,000 &middot; scoped project, based on complexity.</div>
          <div class="cta-link">
            <a href="/start">See how a systems build starts &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-label">Tier 3 &middot; Operator retainer</div>
          <div class="card-title">Embedded systems &amp; decision support.</div>
          <p class="card-body">
            Ongoing partner for founders who need a systems-focused operator in their corner. We steward workflows, help
            sequence major decisions, and keep the operating record current.
          </p>
          <div class="price-line">$2,500&ndash;$5,000 / month &middot; 3-month minimum.</div>
          <div class="cta-link">
            <a href="/start">See how a retainer starts &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Ecosystem connections -->
  <section id="ecosystem" class="section section--tight section--panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">ECOSYSTEM CONNECTIONS</div>
      <h2>Consulting as one lane in a larger system.</h2>
      <p>
        Texas Movement Consulting is one lane inside Texas Movement International. It connects directly to Media for
        documentation and signal, to Performance and Health when systems touch the physical layer, and to Distribution
        when IP defense and platform ops are part of the work.
      </p>
      <p>
        The point is not to treat consulting as a separate agency. The point is to make consulting output compound with
        the rest of Texas Movement&mdash;so systems, content, physical training, and IP defense all line up.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Early Childhood AI Toolkit -->
  <section id="early-childhood" class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">EARLY CHILDHOOD &middot; AI TOOLKIT</div>
        <h2>Play-based AI tools for daycare and early childhood programs.</h2>
        <p>
          Texas Movement Consulting also supports early childhood leaders with a practical AI toolkit built for real
          daycare and preschool classrooms. It helps directors and teachers generate weekly curriculum, theme-based
          activities, and family updates in minutes, without needing to become AI experts.
        </p>
        <p>
          The toolkit is play-based, safety-first, and inclusive of diverse families and abilities. It is designed so a
          first-year teacher and a 20-year veteran can both copy a prompt, add their room details, and get ready-to-run
          plans that fit their program&rsquo;s standards.
        </p>
        <p class="cta-link">
          <a href="/early-childhood-ai-toolkit"> View the Early Childhood AI Toolkit &rarr; </a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="panel-highlight">
        <h3>What&rsquo;s inside the toolkit.</h3>
        <p>The Early Childhood AI Toolkit includes three core tools:</p>
        <p>
          A <strong>Weekly Curriculum Generator</strong> that turns a single theme and age group into a full, play-based
          week of learning.
        </p>
        <p>
          A <strong>Theme-Based Activity Builder</strong> that fills any theme with varied circle, center, movement, and
          art/sensory activities.
        </p>
        <p>
          An <strong>Adaptation &amp; Parent Communication assistant</strong> that adapts plans for every child and
          produces warm, plain-language family updates.
        </p>
        <p class="cta-link">
          <a href="/early-childhood-ai-toolkit"> Launch the toolkit for your center &rarr; </a>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" class="section section--tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions.</h2>
      <div class="faq-grid">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What kind of work is this?</h3>
          <p>
            Strategy, systems design, AI-assisted workflows, and decision support for founders and operators. The
            output is a system and a record, not just slides.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Who is it a fit for?</h3>
          <p>
            Founders, operators, and teams with real stakes, clear-enough briefs, and a willingness to implement. It is
            not a fit for vague or purely speculative work.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Do you provide legal or tax advice?</h3>
          <p>
            No. Work stays inside systems and operations. It supports your counsel; it does not replace legal, tax, or
            medical advice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How does an engagement start?</h3>
          <p>
            Every engagement is meant to begin with a scoped brief and a 30-Day Systems &amp; AI Diagnostic, which sets
            baselines, constraints, and priorities before any deeper work. Online diagnostic intake is opening soon
            &mdash; see <a href="/start">Start a diagnostic</a> for the current status.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How is this different from generic consulting?</h3>
          <p>
            It is systems-first, documented, and built to compound with the rest of Texas Movement rather than sit as a
            disconnected project.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Where should I go for keynote speaking?</h3>
          <p>
            Keynote and live speaking runs through
            <a href={PROPERTIES.founder.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AlexanderMathai.com</a>.
            Consulting work and keynotes share the same systems lens and standards.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Start -->
  <section id="start" class="section section--tight section--panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">GET STARTED</div>
      <h2>Start with a diagnostic.</h2>
      <p>
        Every engagement is built around a short scoped brief: context, constraints, and what a good outcome looks
        like. Diagnostic intake isn&rsquo;t open for live submissions on this site yet.
      </p>
      <p class="cta-link">
        <a href="/start">See the current status of diagnostic intake &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
